```python
load(
    dataset,
    scale=None,
    years=None,
    variables=None,
    wide=None,
    geometry=False,
    names=False,
    groups=None,
    ref=None,
)
```

Load a dataset as a panel: one row per unit (``geo_id``) and year.

## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}

| Name      | Type        | Description                                                                                                                            | Default    |
|-----------|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|
| dataset   | str         | Dataset id (see ``geo.datasets()``)                                                                                                    | _required_ |
| scale     | str \| None | Scale to load; defaults to the dataset's native scale                                                                                  | `None`     |
| years     |             | An int, a list of ints, or a ``(first, last)`` range (inclusive)                                                                       | `None`     |
| variables |             | A variable or list of variables to keep (``geo_id`` and ``year`` are always kept); ``geo.search()`` and ``geo.dictionary()`` list them | `None`     |
| wide      | str \| None | A variable name; returns one row per unit with one column per year (``<variable><year>``)                                              | `None`     |
| geometry  | bool        | Attach unit boundaries (and names) and return a GeoDataFrame                                                                           | `False`    |
| names     | bool        | Add the unit ``name``                                                                                                                  | `False`    |
| groups    |             | Coarser scales whose unit names to add as columns, e.g. ``["department"]`` adds a ``department`` column (implies ``names``)            | `None`     |
| ref       | str \| None | Git branch, tag or commit to read from GitHub (default: local checkout or ``main``)                                                    | `None`     |

## Notes {.doc-section .doc-section-notes}

Raises ``ValueError`` for unknown variables, and for years that have no rows
(listing the years the dataset has).

## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}

```python
!pip install -q geo4bolivia
import geo4bolivia as geo
import plotly.express as px

df = geo.load("sdg05", variables=["index_sdg5"], years=[2012, 2024],
              groups=["department"])
px.histogram(df, x="index_sdg5", color="year", barmode="overlay",
             labels=geo.labels(df), title="Gender equality index")
```

